🔹 Medallion layers (AWS-aligned)

📁 Landing

Scope: Source → S3 only
(Used for API, DB2, RDS, vendor feeds, etc.)

Purpose
	•	First stop for data coming into AWS
	•	Raw copy for traceability & replays
	•	No Spark, no Delta, no joins

What goes here
	•	API responses (JSON / CSV)
	•	DB2 → S3 extracts
	•	Vendor files (Signify, claims feeds)
	•	Scheduled batch dumps

Rules
	•	No transformations
	•	No schema enforcement
	•	Immutable files

Example

API / DB2 / RDS
      ↓
S3 (landing bucket)

🔑 Landing is AWS infrastructure, not analytics.

⸻

📁 Bronze

Scope: S3 → Delta (raw structured)

Purpose
	•	Convert raw files into Delta tables
	•	Apply schema once
	•	Add ingestion metadata

What happens
	•	Read from S3 landing
	•	Write to Delta (bronze schema)
	•	Append-only

Allowed
	•	Schema inference
	•	Metadata columns (ingest_ts, batch_id)
	•	CDC ingestion

Not allowed
	•	Joins
	•	Business rules

⸻

📁 Silver

Scope: Clean & conform

Purpose
	•	Make data reliable and usable
	•	Entity-level tables

What happens
	•	Deduplication
	•	Type casting
	•	Standardized IDs
	•	Light joins (reference tables)

Examples
	•	One row per member
	•	Clean HHV completed table
	•	Claims conformed by member + DOS

⸻

📁 Gold

Scope: Business & analytics

Purpose
	•	Metrics, KPIs, dashboards

What happens
	•	Aggregations
	•	Filters by business rules
	•	Final reporting grain

Examples
	•	HHV → Claim conversion %
	•	Missing claims by market
	•	Monthly summaries

⸻

